WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.840
 Once we've created a workspace 
  in RStudio Cloud, a great next 

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.440
 step is to add any co-instructors 
  and teaching assistants to the space 

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.160
 to help us get everything set up from 
  within our workspace. 

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.160
 We click on the members tab at the top,  

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:20.720
 where by default we see any current 
  members already in the workspace. 

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.720
 We can also click on invitations 
  to see the status 

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.880
 of any pending invitations 
  that we've sent. 

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.320
 If we click on the add member 
  button, we see a pop 

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.720
 up asking us for the new members' 
  email address, role, 

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:36.200
 and any additional text 
  we wish to include in the invite. 

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.320
 One thing we need to think about 
  here is what role 

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:42.520
 we'd like to add our co-instructors 
  and teaching assistants as. 

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.640
 Inviting someone as a moderator  

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.280
 allows that person to access 
  all of the projects within a workspace. 

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:51.800
 Whereas if we add them 
  as an administrator, 

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:53.520
 they will also have the ability  

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.120
 to add and remove students 
  as well as change the workspace settings. 

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:00.560
 Whatever we choose, 
  we aren't locked into that option forever. 

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.640
 Let's look here where I've added myself 
  as a member to our data 

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:06.960
 visualization workspace.  

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:10.160
 I can change my role 
  by clicking on the dropdown menu 

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.080
 and choosing an updated role 
  for any member within the workspace. 

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.200
 Adding members in this way is great 

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.960
 when we want to add 
  workspace members one by one. 

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:24.520
 Check out our Inviting Learners video 
  for ways to add multiple members at once. 

